<graph edgedefault="undirected"><node id="AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0">
  <data key="d0">AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0 is an anion exchange membrane electrolyser product manufactured by Enapter, with documented technical specifications.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e06535e825223474477846fa321f1ad0</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter">
  <data key="d0">Enapter</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Enapter is the company that manufactures the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0.&lt;SEP&gt;Enapter is the manufacturer of the EL40 hydrogen electrolyzer and the developer of its associated Energy Management System (EMS).</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e06535e825223474477846fa321f1ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Technical Specifications">
  <data key="d0">Technical Specifications</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Technical specifications are the documented technical parameters of the AEM Electrolyser EL 4.0, presented in a table format.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-e06535e825223474477846fa321f1ad0</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625047</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="table_a01099d4a0f1356cd04b854534af4fb2">
  <data key="d0">table_a01099d4a0f1356cd04b854534af4fb2</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">Table content: {'type': 'table', 'img_path': 'C:\\Users\\gauva\\Desktop\\raganything-hazop\\output\\Enapter_Datashe</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625056</data>
</node>
<node id="El40">
  <data key="d0">El40</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The EL40 is a hydrogen electrolyzer device manufactured by Enapter, producing up to 500 NL/h of hydrogen with output pressures up to 35 barg, weighing 42 kg and measuring 482 mm × 635 mm × 266 mm.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter Ems">
  <data key="d0">Enapter Ems</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enapter EMS (Energy Management System) is a fully automatic control and monitoring system for the EL40, operating via 2.4 GHz Wi-Fi, Bluetooth, and Modbus TCP over Ethernet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625493</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Water Electrolysis">
  <data key="d0">Water Electrolysis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Water electrolysis is the electrochemical process used by the EL40 to produce hydrogen gas, consuming approximately 420 mL/h of water at 25 °C.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrogen">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen is the gaseous output of the EL40 electrolyzer, with purity levels of 99.9% at 35 barg and 98.8% at 8 barg, measured by H₂O and O₂ content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Astm D1193-06">
  <data key="d0">Astm D1193-06</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">ASTM D1193-06 is a water quality standard specifying Type IV (minimum) or Type II/III (recommended) conductivity levels for water input to the EL40 electrolyzer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ce Mark">
  <data key="d0">Ce Mark</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The CE Mark is a conformity certification for the EL40, granted according to the Machine Directive 2006/42/CE.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ukca Mark">
  <data key="d0">Ukca Mark</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The UKCA Mark is a conformity certification for the EL40, granted according to the Supply Machinery (Safety) Regulations 2008.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Csa/Ansi B22734:2023">
  <data key="d0">Csa/Ansi B22734:2023</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">CSA/ANSI B22734:2023 Ed.1 is a standard for Hydrogen Generators Using Water Electrolysis covering industrial, commercial, and residential applications, to which the EL40 conforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Modbus Tcp">
  <data key="d0">Modbus Tcp</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Modbus TCP is a communication protocol used by the Enapter EMS for control and monitoring of the EL40 over Ethernet.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Enapter Datasheet El40">
  <data key="d0">Enapter Datasheet El40</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Enapter Datasheet EL40 is a technical specification document containing detailed parameters including production rate, purity, power consumption, dimensions, and conformity certifications for the EL40 device.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Wi-Fi">
  <data key="d0">Wi-Fi</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wi-Fi (2.4 GHz) is a wireless connectivity method used by the Enapter EMS for remote control and monitoring of the EL40.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bluetooth">
  <data key="d0">Bluetooth</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Bluetooth is a wireless connectivity method used by the Enapter EMS for local control and monitoring of the EL40.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Machine Directive 2006/42/Ce">
  <data key="d0">Machine Directive 2006/42/Ce</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Machine Directive 2006/42/CE is an EU regulatory framework that forms the basis for the CE Mark certification of the EL40 electrolyzer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supply Machinery (Safety) Regulations 2008">
  <data key="d0">Supply Machinery (Safety) Regulations 2008</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Supply Machinery (Safety) Regulations 2008 is a UK regulatory framework that forms the basis for the UKCA Mark certification of the EL40 electrolyzer.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-ccc2a7da10d8d7b6995d26a2b7d87a82</data>
  <data key="d4">Enapter_Datasheet_EL40_EN.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1790625502</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
